## 1. New hazard dialogue

When the player starts the level that introduces a hazard (`HAZ.find(h => h.lv === n)`), show a dialogue before the run begins:

- **Eyebrow:** `new hazard` (same mono uppercase eyebrow style).
- **Show the hazard itself:** above the title, show a small live preview of the hazard so the player sees exactly what it looks like in the game before they meet it. Draw it with the game's own render code (`js/render.js`), in the current level's theme colours, on a small canvas inside the card (about 220×140 CSS px, 2× for sharp screens). Do not use the flat `docs/hazards/*.svg` icons for this; the player must recognise the real thing when it scrolls in.
  - Ideally it is a tiny looping demo: the runner meets the hazard and uses it correctly (bounces on the Bloom, jumps through the Halo and air-jumps, rolls onto the Coil and launches, etc.), so the picture explains the rule along with the text. A short scripted loop of 2–3 seconds is enough. If a full demo is too much for a hazard, show the hazard on its own on a bit of ground with its idle animation (Prism spinning, Fade tiles, zone tint with its bubbles/chevrons/wavy lines).
  - Keep the preview separate from the frozen main game: it must not advance the real sim, clock or music.
  - Stop its `requestAnimationFrame` loop when the card closes. With `prefers-reduced-motion`, show one still frame instead of the loop.
- **Title:** the hazard name (e.g. `BLOOM`), with the hazard colour used as an accent (underline, icon glow or a coloured dot — keep the title text readable).
- **Body:** the explanation from the table below. Use "roll" (see section 4).
- **One button:** `Understood`, styled `solid`. `Enter` must also trigger it (already handled by `G.cardUp` + `cardActs[0]`).

### Freezing

The game must be fully frozen while the dialogue is up: no music, no clock, no runner movement, no input reaching the sim.

- Split `beginRun` so that on the intro level the state and level are set up and the first frame is drawn (the runner standing at the start), but `MUSIC.start()` and `clock.start()` are **not** called yet. Use a distinct mode such as `G.mode = "intro"` so the jump/roll key and pointer handlers (which check `G.mode === "play"`) ignore input, and the frame loop doesn't advance the sim.
- Clicking `Understood` (or pressing Enter) hides the card and the objective box, sets `G.mode = "play"`, then starts the music and clock exactly as `beginRun` does today, so the run starts in sync from beat 0.
- Make sure `Escape`, tab hiding (`visibilitychange`) and window `blur` don't break this: `pauseGame()` must not open a Paused card on top of the intro card, and coming back to the tab must not start the music.
- Show it once per `startLevel(n)` of that level (i.e. when entering the level from home, "next level" or "replay"), **not** on restarts after dying or from the Paused menu (`beginRun(false)`).
- The home attract-mode demo must never show it.

